  "description": "Use when converting a PDF, scanned document, slide deck, or DOCX into Markdown that must stay faithful to the source — a paper, thesis, standard, datasheet, SDK guide, or manual that will be read, grepped, cited, or diffed later. Use when the source carries equations, tables, figures with captions, numbered sections, or a bibliography. Use when the user says convert to markdown, extract this paper, turn this PDF into docs, make this reference greppable, or asks for structure such as an index plus per-chapter files plus assets. Also use when converting a spreadsheet (.xlsx, .csv, Google Sheet) or a diagram file (draw.io, mxGraph) into Markdown tables or a Mermaid flow. Also use when reviewing or repairing a conversion someone else produced.",
